From 1d3b854e7b95318b67afd2dc16b8ff5fc060443a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Sep 2024 11:24:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip: stm32mp-exti: Add support of wake-up path for S2Idle

For S2Idle support in STM32MP2 family, the EXTI1 device is part of
the CpuIdle PSCI power domain RET_PD, as indicated in the device
tree.
The domain RET_PD supports the flag GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP since
commit bfd5859709ee ("cpuidle: psci: Activate GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP
with OSI").
Since EXTI1 wake-up is not functional with reduced VDDCore, use
the wake-up path API device_set_wakeup_path() to manage the low
power mode restrictions.

This lets the power domain core code know that the domain RET_PD
should not be powered off during system suspend S2Idle (with PSCI
OSI support) and the LPLV-Stop1 mode is not allowed when a
wake-up interrupt is activated on the EXTI instance.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-stm32mp-exti.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-stm32mp-exti.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-stm32mp-exti.c
@@ -289,6 +289,10 @@ static void stm32mp_chip_suspend(struct
 	chip_data->ftsr_cache = readl_relaxed(base + bank->ftsr_ofst);
 
 	writel_relaxed(wake_active, base + bank->imr_ofst);
+
+	/* wakeup for IRQ power domain for S2IDLE */
+	if (wake_active)
+		device_set_wakeup_path(chip_data->host_data->dev);
 }
 
 static void stm32mp_chip_resume(struct stm32mp_exti_chip_data *chip_data, u32 mask_cache)
